//
// Host-only audit of the shared verify driver's command line.
//
// `[2026-08-12]` verify_runner.py parsed a seed option and never read it, so a
// verification invoked with one was NOT seeded by it and any reproducibility
// claim resting on it was empty -- while the run passed and looked seeded. This
// is the gate all ten shipped models pass through, which is what made it the
// highest-stakes instance of that day's pattern: a mechanism that reads as
// present, does nothing, and produces a green result rather than a wrong one.
//
// The option was removed rather than wired, because nothing the gate reaches
// consumes randomness -- both decode paths are greedy, weights come from a
// checkpoint, tokenization and the top-k comparison are deterministic. That was
// measured, not assumed: an ast walk of the driver's repo-local import closure
// (verify_runner plus all ten verify_adapter modules) puts every RNG site
// inside a builder's __main__ self-test block or inside synthetic_weights(),
// which has zero call sites anywhere in the tree.
//
// What runs here is the audit that keeps the next one from landing: every flag
// the driver parses must be read somewhere in the same module. It PARSES the
// driver and never imports it -- no numpy, no torch, no transformers, no XRT --
// so it needs neither `ryzen_ai_npu2` nor `peano` and costs milliseconds. Its
// own negative control runs on every invocation: a dead flag is injected into a
// copy of the real source text and the same walk must find it, so an audit that
// has stopped being able to detect one fails rather than reporting zero.
//
// There is deliberately no `make` target for this arm, matching the study host
// suite and the ffn_resident emulation arm; the two lit-only arms in this tree
// are lit-only on purpose.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose registers as a directive. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/test_verify_runner.py | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: PASS  test_a_stored_flag_does_not_count_as_read
// CHECK: PASS  test_no_flag_is_parsed_and_never_read
// CHECK: PASS  test_the_audit_can_actually_fail
// CHECK: PASS  test_the_driver_parses_flags_at_all
// CHECK: PASS  test_the_gate_decodes_greedily_which_is_why_no_seed_is_needed
// CHECK: PASS  test_the_greedy_check_can_actually_fail
// CHECK: PASS  test_the_seed_flag_is_gone_and_stays_gone
// CHECK: verify runner tests: 7/7 passed
//
// The Llama drivers' prompt-length seam (llama32_1b/test_prompt_len.py): the
// real prompt length must reach the prefill, since instruct templates carry EOS
// inside the prompt.
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../llama32_1b/test_prompt_len.py | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLEN
// PLEN: PASS  llama32_1b: run_once -> generate carries prompt_len=7
// PLEN: PASS  llama32_1b_int4: run_once -> generate carries prompt_len=7
// PLEN: prompt_len seam tests: 2/2 passed
